\title{Pre-PhD (2017-2019)}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2025-09-03}

\p{
    I started working in crypto during the two years between my [MSc](dhsorens-msc) and my
    [PhD](dhsorens-phd).
    My first job was at a small, Utah-based crypto startup called Pyrofex, which was mostly
    providing consulting services to the [RChain co-op](https://github.com/dhsorens/rchain) at the
    time.
    I was tasked with [building the formal semantics for
    rholang](https://github.com/dhsorens/rholang), the smart contracting language on RChain, in [K
    Framework](dhsorens-001D) in order to formally verify rholang contracts down the line.
}

\p{
    RChain, famously, encountered sudden and urgent financial problems because of a questionable set
    of decisions from the co-op's president, Greg Meredith, which necessitated a split between
    RChain and Pyrofex.
    We then pivoted to consensus-level research, designed our own layer-one blockchain and
    [consensus protocol](/docs/Casanova.pdf).
}

\p{
    Sadly, we ran out of money, and I had to look for a new job for the few months before my PhD
    started.
    I took a short internship with Digital Asset, working in Zurich and New York, and [implementing
    an experimental currency](/docs/cantoncoin.pdf) on their blockchain-esque project Canton.
}